          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia’s solo follows Mateo’s reluctance, but repeated dialogue and the unexplained drums left on the shelf make the ending feel unfinished.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia chooses a solo and accepts Mateo’s choice, though this is stated rather than dramatized; the final shelf image does little to resolve the moment.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000058\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"The solo is a plausible response to Mateo’s hesitation, but his repeated refusal and the drums left on the shelf make for a thin, unresolved ending.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia accepts Mateo’s choice after performing alone, but the acceptance is only reported and the ending offers little sense of closure.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000036\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":7,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":5,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Mateo’s eventual offer changes the outcome into a private duet, giving the story a clearer resolution, though the repeated solo setup and shelf image feel mechanical.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":6,\"style\":4,\"grammar\":8,\"storytelling\":4,\"overall\":5},\"note\":\"Nia responds to Mateo’s hesitation with a solo, but the repeated refusal and final shelf detail leave the scene static and incomplete.\",\"group_id\":0}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":2,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":2,\"language\":1,\"overall\":2},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All six stories begin with the same hoped-for duet, Mateo’s reluctance, and Nia’s solo choice. Five (s000014, s000028, s000058, s000023, s000017) end with the solo and drums on the shelf; s000036 alone changes the causal outcome when Mateo later agrees to a private duet. Wording varies only slightly, so the set has little plot or language diversity.\" ,\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Mateo is not ready for a duet, so Nia performs a solo; the story ends without a shared performance.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"After Nia performs a solo, Mateo proposes playing privately, and they resolve the hesitation by playing a duet together.\"}] }",
